#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:4
msgid "Step 5: Instrumentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:8
msgid ""
"This step extends :ref:`Step 3 <CTest Dashboard Step 3>` by "
"enabling :manual:`instrumentation <cmake-instrumentation(7)>`, which records "
"the time taken by each configure, build, and test command and submits it to "
"CDash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:13
msgid "Step5/submit.cmake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:13
msgid ""
"# Enable instrumentation.  This is often set by the calling environment\n"
"# instead, such as a CI job definition.\n"
"set(ENV{CTEST_USE_INSTRUMENTATION} \"ON\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:18
msgid ""
"Setting the :envvar:`CTEST_USE_INSTRUMENTATION` environment variable before "
"the dashboard steps run enables instrumentation.  The rest of the script is "
"the same as Step 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:22
msgid ""
"The variable can also be set by the environment that runs the script, such "
"as a CI job definition.  This lets the same script run with or without "
"instrumentation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:26
msgid "CTEST_USE_INSTRUMENTATION=ON ctest -S Step5/submit.cmake -V"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:30
msgid ""
"See the :manual:`cmake-instrumentation(7)` manual for details about the data "
"that is submitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:34
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Instrumentation.rst:36
msgid "The same as :ref:`Step 3 <CTest Dashboard Step 3>`."
msgstr ""
